[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue with one fix. Its reports show two causes,
and each now has a ticket of its own. Engineering closed #4471 on 05 Oct.

<Callout kind="warn">
Two problems, not one. The parser fix closed one of them. The other ended when its form was
retired, not because a fix shipped.
</Callout>

## The problems

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

| cause | ticket | outcome |
|---|---|---|
| `parser` | [#1](https://github.com/jpalmowski/support-kb/issues/1) | fixed: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` |
| `hint` | [#2](https://github.com/jpalmowski/support-kb/issues/2) | won't fix: booking-v3 form retired |

- **Shared parser reads month first.** Every tenant writes the day first. The parser swaps day and
  month on any date with a day of 12 or less: a booking for 7 April becomes an invite for 4 July.
  This is the bug #4471 is named for.
- **booking-v3 hint says MM/DD.** The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field,
  then reads the field day first. People type what the hint says, and the date flips before it
  reaches the parser. The parser fix does not touch it; retiring the form ends it.

The reports the desk read as a one-day move are counted under `parser`, where their tenant files
them. A ticket opened for them ([#3](https://github.com/jpalmowski/support-kb/issues/3)) is
closed as a duplicate of #1.

## How the reports are placed

A report's cause comes from where it was made, not from its subject line or its intake tag:

1. Take each report once. The export repeats some reports across pages, so count by id.
2. Tenant and channel decide the cause (`causes.ts`): a day-first tenant using the booking-v3
   form has the hint cause. Every other report from a day-first tenant has the parser cause.

The intake tag is a guess from the reporter's browser. It disagrees with the cause on reports in
both directions, so it does not decide the ticket.

## What changes for the desk

- Two reports are duplicates when they share a **cause**, not a subject. The
  [dedupe explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe) shows subject and cause disagreeing in every case it
  tests. [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) (merge on subject) put both
  causes in #4471, and it is stale. It needs a new decision record to replace it.
- Before merging a date report, check the tenant and the channel.

